Built with [QiForge](https://github.com/ixoworld/qiforge) on top of `@ixo/oracle-runtime`.

## Quickstart

```bash
pnpm install
cp .env.example .env       # fill in MATRIX_*, ORACLE_ENTITY_DID, LLM keys
pnpm dev                   # tsx watch src/main.ts
```

The oracle listens on `PORT` (default 3000).

## Adding a plugin

```bash
qiforge-cli plugin new my-plugin
```

Scaffolds `src/plugins/my-plugin/` with a class skeleton + tests. Register the
generated plugin in `src/main.ts`:

```ts
import { MyPluginPlugin } from './plugins/my-plugin/my-plugin.plugin.js';

await createOracleApp({
  config,
  plugins: [new EditorPlugin({ matrixClient }), new MyPluginPlugin()],
});
```

## Layout

```
src/
├── main.ts       # bootstrap — createOracleApp + listen
├── config.ts     # oracle identity + system prompt
└── plugins/      # your custom plugins
.env              # secrets — never commit
```

## Scripts

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` | Hot-reload dev server (tsx watch). |
| `pnpm build` | Compile TypeScript → `dist/`. |
| `pnpm start` | Run the compiled build. |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Type-check without emit. |
| `pnpm test` | Run unit tests. |
